<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.9.0: Lesson Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00203</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.9.0: Lesson Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>dd7f12e2-509a-4a44-bcc0-312e0b267fa7</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, you will practice solving for a specific variable to obtain an expression defined in terms of the other variables. Through the lesson’s activities you will see that this process allows you to solve problems more efficiently.</para>
<para>When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list>
  <item>Solve an equation for one of the variables.</item>
</list>
<para><span>Here are the <emphasis>activities </emphasis>that will help you reach those goals:</span></para>
<list>
  <item>1.9.1: Rearranging an Equation in Three Variables</item>
  <item>1.9.2: Writing an Equation to Represent a Constraint<list>
      <item>1.9.2: Self Check </item>
      <item>1.9.2: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>1.9.3: Writing and Rearranging Equations in Two Variables<list>
      <item>1.9.3: Self Check </item>
      <item>1.9.3: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>1.9.4: Solving for a Specified Variable</item>
</list>
<para>After that, you'll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
<list>
  <item>1.9.5: Practice</item>
  <item>1.9.6: Lesson Summary</item>
</list></section>
</content>
</document>
